  "text": "Fixed the off-by-one in `parse_grid()`'s loop bound (`gridtools/io.py:13`): `range(0, len(edges) - 2)` was dropping the last valid pair (and two when the count was odd), so I changed it to `range(0, len(edges) - 1)`, which is the correct bound for producing `n - 1` cells from `n` edges. All 3 tests in `tests/test_io.py` now pass."
